{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Local Criterion for Projectivity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Local Criterion for Projectivity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"local criterion for projectivity local criterion for projectivity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Local Criterion for Projectivity.md","fileName":"Local Criterion for Projectivity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Local Criterion for Projectivity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Projective Flat and Injective Modules]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Local Property","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Local Criterion for Projectivity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Local Criterion for Projectivity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"local criterion for projectivity local criterion for projectivity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Local Criterion for Projectivity.md","fileName":"Local Criterion for Projectivity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Local Criterion for Projectivity","heading":"Local Criterion for Projectivity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A finitely presented module P is projective if and only if P_p is projective over R_p for every prime ideal p; equivalently, it is enough to test every maximal ideal. Under the source's Noetherian finite-generation hypotheses, the localized modules are free.\n\nThe criterion makes projectivity a [[Local Property]]. Finite presentation ensures that maps and relations behave well enough under localization to recover the global splitting.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Projective Flat and Injective Modules","Local Property","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full N